---
source: tests/regression.rs
expression: sandbox.run(&arguments)
---
exit code: 0
--- stdout
Run any AI coding agent in a hardened, disposable container, with your project mounted where you can see every change.

Usage: casulo <COMMAND>

Commands:
  new       Create a project: clone a repository and prepare its environment
  doctor    Check that git and the container runtime are ready, and how to fix them
  setup     Create ~/.casulo with documented defaults, then install or fix what casulo needs, asking before each command
  build     Generate the project's Dockerfile for a harness and build the image
  run       Run the agent in a hardened container with the workspace mounted
  shell     Open a bash shell in the same container the agent runs in
  harness   Work with harnesses, the descriptions of how to install and run each agent
  compose   Work with the services of the project's docker compose file
  describe  Show details of a resource, such as the project's memory
  index     Update an index, such as the project's memory of its code
  search    Search the project's memory, the same way agents do with recall
  config    Open the global casulo.toml, or a project's, in your editor
  add       Create a subagent, skill, MCP server or workflow from a template, in your editor
  edit      Change a subagent, skill, MCP server or workflow in your editor
  list      List your subagents, skills, MCP servers and workflows, or the project's memory notes
  promote   Promote a branch note of the project's memory to a general one
  stop      Stop a running service, such as the project's memory server
  delete    Delete a subagent, skill, MCP server or workflow
  home      Print the casulo home directory
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
--- stderr
